      "source": [
        "When users have very few ratings (e.g. 10), and their ratings span polarized items (e.g., highly rating their favorite genre and heavily downvoting their least-favorite), their personal mean becomes highly biased and unrepresentative. In such cases, the global mean serves as a smoother and more robust default predictor than a highly noisy individual mean."
      ],
      "id": "1jnOOg52XEhU"
    },
